    "summary": "Electrified Warfield set featuring Terrapin, Althea and a Foxy Lady tease",
    "blurb": "The February 16, 1982 Warfield performance launches a soaring Terrapin Station that segues into Althea, delivers a crowd‑pleasing Peggy‑O, and ventures into an exploratory Space punctuated by a brief Foxy Lady tease. Keyboard textures shimmer on Friend Of The Devil, while the rhythm section propels the flow despite muddy audience tape quality.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Warfield on this early‑1982 night is a cohesively locked‑in Dead run that rides the band's electrified groove. Set 1 builds momentum with Shakedown Street and a crisp rendition of Friend Of The Devil, then rolls into an upbeat Peggy‑O that still manages to cut through the murky tape. The second set shines brightest: China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider launches into a blazing Playing In The Band → Terrapin Station sequence that feels both adventurous and grounded, while the Drums/Space segment sprinkles in a whimsical Foxy Lady tease before launching into an extended Truckin' jam. The show closes with the familiar swing of Good Lovin’ and a gentle encore of Don't Ease Me In. Though the recording is an audience capture with noticeable hiss and bass that’s hard to isolate, it preserves the band’s inspired interplay and makes this performance worth a spin for any Warfield‑era collector.",
